(pot)
(bowl)

::instructions

(water) <boil, fully>
Meanwhile [
    (spices) <put, in (pot)>
    (spaghetti) <place, on top of the spices>
]
(water) <pour, boiling water over the spaghetti> ?= spaghetti softened enough to immerse fully
{spaghetti and water} <mix, thoroughly with the spices>
If needed, add (salt) and (pepper).
(pot) <place, on the stove>
(spaghetti) <boil, ~8m> ?= fully cooked when tasted
Meanwhile [
    (spaghetti) <stir, every 1-2m>
    Optional [
        Cook (egg) and/or (bacon) while the spaghetti cooks, as suggested by the source.
    ]
]
# The source says cooking should take no more than eight minutes; taste one piece at a time to check.
(spaghetti) <strain, water from the pot, keeping spaghetti in the pot>
Before returning the pot to the stove:
(spaghetti) + (extra virgin olive oil)
    <mix>
Optional [
    Add (bacon) or (turkey) now if using them.
]
(pot) <return, to the stove>
While stirring, add (tomato addition).
(spaghetti) <mix, 1m, avoiding sticking to the pot>
    <pour, into (bowl)>
# Enjoy!

::notes

The introduction suggests optional eggs and/or bacon cooked while spaghetti boils. The later method mentions bacon or turkey at the oil stage. These source options are retained without inventing an egg-placement step.

::story

A quick breakfast spaghetti recipe that covers a healthy amount of carbs, fat, and spices. Eggs and/or bacon can be added to cover some protein, you should cook those while the boiler is cooking the spaghetti for time efficiency.


